{"ticker":"HCA","updated":"2026-11-07T00:00:00Z","profile":{"longName":"HCA Healthcare, Inc.","shortName":"HCA Healthcare, Inc.","sector":"Healthcare","industry":"Medical Care Facilities","country":"United States","website":"https://www.hcahealthcare.com","fullTimeEmployees":230000,"marketCap":103399694336,"trailingPE":16.417578,"forwardPE":15.821736,"priceToSalesTrailing12Months":1.3138294,"pegRatio":1.55,"targetMeanPrice":475.45456,"targetHighPrice":550.0,"targetLowPrice":380.0,"numberOfAnalystOpinions":22,"recommendationKey":"buy","revenueGrowth":0.036,"earningsGrowth":0.045,"grossMargins":0.42755002,"operatingMargins":0.14832,"profitMargins":0.0861,"totalRevenue":78701002752,"beta":1.101,"fiftyTwoWeekHigh":556.52,"fiftyTwoWeekLow":353.99,"currency":"USD","exchange":"NYQ","quoteType":"EQUITY","dividendYield":0.61},"summary":"HCA Healthcare, Inc., through its subsidiaries, provides health care services in the United States. The company owns, manages, and operates hospitals, ASCs, freestanding emergency care facilities, urgent care facilities, walk-in clinics, diagnostic and imaging centers, radiation and oncology therapy centers, as well as rehabilitation and physical therapy centers, physician practices, home health agencies, hospices, outpatient physical therapy providers, home and community-based services providers, and various other facilities. Its general and acute care hospitals offer medical and surgical services, including inpatient care, intensive care, cardiac care, diagnostic services, and emergency services; and outpatient services, such as outpatient surgery, laboratory, radiology, respiratory therapy, cardiology, and physical therapy. The company was formerly known as HCA Holdings, Inc. HCA Healthcare, Inc. was founded in 1968 and is headquartered in Nashville, Tennessee.","summary_zh":"HCA Healthcare, Inc. 透過其子公司在美國提供醫療保健服務。該公司擁有、管理和經營醫院、ASC、獨立緊急護理設施、緊急護理設施、預約診所、診斷和影像中心、放射和腫瘤治療中心，以及復健和物理治療中心、醫生診所、家庭保健機構、臨終關懷醫院、門診物理治療提供者、家庭和社區服務提供者以及各種其他設施。其普通科和急診醫院提